# 5 Summary

1. −¼F² has no inverse because of residual gauge freedom.

2. ℒ_gf=−(∂·A)²/(2ξ) makes the kinetic operator invertible.

3. D_μν=−i[g_μν−(1−ξ)k_μk_ν/k²]/(k²+iε); ξ=1 is Feynman gauge, ξ=0 is Landau gauge.

4. Independence of ξ is Lesson 71, not an algebraic identity of this propagator alone.

